    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d144">

                <pb facs="0245" n="143" xml:id="pg143"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/539</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Embassy to the
                            Department of State
                    </hi><anchor n="92" xml:id="d144-f1"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1935-11-07">undated</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>In reply to the United States Government’s enquiry,<anchor n="93"
                        xml:id="d144-f2"/> His Majesty’s Government in the United Kingdom desire to
                    explain that the attitude which the Japanese Government may be expected to adopt
                    at the forthcoming Naval Conference was defined in an oral communication made by
                    the Japanese Chargé d’Affaires in London on the 18th October,<anchor n="94"
                        xml:id="d144-f3"/> of which the substance was subsequently given to the
                    United States Chargé d’Affaires. The terms of this communication were as set out
                    in the annexed separate memorandum.</p>
                <p>The attitude of His Majesty’s Government towards the Japanese proposals remains
                    as indicated to the representatives of the United States Government during the
                    conversations which took place last year. The Japanese representatives were
                    similarly informed of the attitude of His Majesty’s Government towards their
                    proposals, particular emphasis being laid on the special responsibilities
                    devolving on the United Kingdom as a result of the deterioration of the
                    political situation in Europe and increased building by many European
                    Powers.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d144-f1" n="92" type="source" xml:id="d144-f1-content">
                <p>Handed to the Under Secretary of State by the British Chargé, November 7,
                    1935.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d144-f2" n="93" xml:id="d144-f2-content">
                <p>See memorandum by the Under Secretary of State, November 1, <ref target="#pg138"
